WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/features/system/components/status/IncidentsCard.tsx — the active-incidents banner on /system-status:

    Gate (web): `const incidents = active?.incidents ?? []; if (incidents.length === 0) return null`. When there
      are no active incidents the WHOLE card collapses (returns null). The web comment calls this the "Empty state".
    Header: <AlertTriangle/> "Active incidents" <Badge variant="warning">{incidents.length}</Badge>  +  a ghost
      "Log incident" button (<Plus/>) that opens the <IncidentForm/> dialog (state `open`).
    List (<ul>): each incident is a <Link to=/system-status/incidents/:id> row:
      • severity glyph + colour — SEVERITY_TONE: minor=AlertCircle/amber, major=AlertTriangle/orange,
        critical=AlertOctagon/red.
      • title (truncate) + <Badge variant={STATUS_BADGE[status]}>{status}</Badge> + severity label (tone text).
        STATUS_BADGE: investigating=danger, identified=warning, monitoring=info, resolved=success.
      • {affected_components.length > 0 && "Affects: {affected_components.join(', ')}"}
      • "Started {relativeFrom(now, started_at)}{updates.length > 1 && ` · ${updates.length} updates`}"
      • trailing <ChevronRight/>.
  Hook   : useIncidents({ activeOnly: true }) (TanStack, refetchInterval 30s) → { incidents, count }. This prompt's
           ONLY listed data source is useIncidents; the create mutation (useCreateIncident) + the IncidentForm
           dialog are a SEPARATE surface.
  Helper (reproduced verbatim — arithmetic is the contract):
           relativeFrom(now, iso): Date.parse → !finite ? "" : let secs = max(0, floor((now - t)/1000));
             secs < 60 ? "just now" : secs < 3600 ? "{floor(secs/60)}m ago" : secs < 86400 ? "{floor(secs/3600)}h ago"
             : "{floor(secs/86400)}d ago".  Magnitudes are bare template-literal integers (NO grouping).
  i18n  : the web source is "anonymous" — it uses hardcoded English literals (no t() calls). Per the native
          no-English-literals rule every literal is promoted to a P1/S10 key (table "IncidentsCard").

