KEY DECISIONS  (no silent drift — disclosed in full)
  EMPTY STATE      The web COLLAPSES to null when incidents.length === 0. Repo engineering rule #6 ("HIDING sections
                   when data is null … must always show with placeholder") + the P4 leaf contract ("every state MUST
                   render — no hidden surfaces / never a blank box") OVERRIDE the web collapse for the native leaf:
                   the surface renders a calm, visible empty state ("No active incidents", checkmark glyph). This is
                   the SAME class of sanctioned leaf elevation the prompt applies to loading/error/stale/offline
                   (states the web also lacks). Documented; not a silent drift.
  SEVERITY COLOUR  The web uses three warm tints (amber/orange/red); the native P1/S9 design system exposes two warm
                   status tokens (statusWarning / statusDanger). Mapping: minor→warning, major→warning,
                   critical→danger — minor vs major stay distinguished by SF Symbol (circle vs triangle) + the
                   severity label text. No raw hex is introduced (token discipline).
  LOG / NAVIGATE   The "Log incident" CTA + the row tap are exposed as INJECTED seams (onLogIncident / onOpenIncident)
                   — the web IncidentsCard composes <IncidentForm/> + <Link/>, but the IncidentForm surface and its
                   useCreateIncident mutation are a SEPARATE prompt (this prompt's only data source is useIncidents).
                   The button + row are fully wired (they invoke the seam); the host provides the destination. Not a
                   stub — standard DI, asserted by tests.

PARITY MAPPING  (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported, no raw hex)
  GlassPanel(ring-amber/30 bg-amber/[.03]) → card with statusWarning.opacity(0.3) ring + statusWarning.opacity(0.04)
                                  fill in the data phase; neutral Color.TS.border in loading/empty/error.
  Badge(variant)                → status: IncidentTagView (capsule fill .15 + stroke .3 at the tone, like TSBadge);
                                  count: shared TSBadge(tone:.warning); severity label: plain tone text (web span).
  lucide AlertCircle/Triangle/Octagon/Plus/ChevronRight → SF Symbols exclamationmark.circle/triangle/octagon.fill /
                                  plus / chevron.right.
  STATUS_BADGE map              → IncidentStatus.tone (investigating=danger, identified=warning, monitoring=info,
                                  resolved=success) — asserted against the web map.
  relativeFrom                  → IncidentsRelative.bucket + IncidentsProjection.relativeLabel (same thresholds, FLOOR,
                                  "just now", bare integers, "" on unparseable).
  affected_components.join      → IncidentsProjection.affectsLine (verbatim join, nil only when the array is empty —
                                  matches the web length>0 guard exactly; no filtering, per the web).
  Button (ghost)                → shared TSButton(variant:.ghost) ; QueryError retry → TSButton(variant:.secondary).
  i18n                          → every string via IncidentsStrings (NSLocalizedString table "IncidentsCard", web
                                  literal as the value: fallback); %@ templates so translators control word order.
  a11y                          → each row is one combined button element with a composed VoiceOver label
                                  ("{title}. {severity} severity. Status: {status}. {affects}. {meta}") + an open
                                  hint; chip / refresh / retry / log labelled; Dynamic Type via tokens; Reduce Motion
                                  via TSFadeIn / TSSkeleton.
  telemetry                     → view.opened surface="IncidentsCard" emitted once on the first presented snapshot.

STATES (every one renders — no hidden surface)
  loading  → skeleton incident rows (the web collapses during load; the leaf keeps the card shape).
  empty    → "No active incidents" with a calm checkmark glyph (web returns null; native leaf renders a visible
             state per rule #6), never a blank box.
  error    → retryable error chrome (P4 leaf addition; the web would collapse on error).
  data     → the active-incident list (glyph + title + status badge + severity label + affects + started/updates
             meta + chevron), with the amber ring emphasis.
  stale    → header chip + banner + one-shot auto-refresh on the live→stale transition.
  offline  → header chip + banner over last-known rows; no auto-refresh.

